Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||04-04-2001||12:17 AM||||Bad things about the ZZ4?? Huh? we have run one in our vette hard for about a year now , track events , puts down over 300hp to the wheels with a modded injection system , beautiful motor. I know a bunch of one lap guys pushing 550hp with zz4's that have never been opened up , just sueprcharged , these guys run harder than you can imagine in the one lap of america. <P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Archie||04-04-2001||01:32 AM||||I've installed more than 25 ZZ4's and more than 20 ZZ3's before that. I'd say my customers have installed more than 100 ZZ engines.<P>No one has had a problem yet.<P>I am currently installing 2 more ZZ4 engines.  Maybe one of the HTD experts can fill us in on these "BAD THINGS".<P>I know that some people who are doing V-8 cars, with kits they've copied, don't have anyone to make the GM balance F/Wheels that the ZZ engines must have. But other than that, I don't know of any problems with the ZZ engines themselves.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000006||Predator||04-04-2001||07:23 AM||||Archie, Are the V8 conversions emmisions legal? I thought about a V8, but got scared off because Georgia is getting harder on emmisions testing.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||04-04-2001||08:38 AM||||a TPI V8 or a carbed motor with an EGR plate would pass emissions. the visual inspection they look for a cat and egr. unless the motor has just CRAZY compression it'll pass NOx. and CO and CO2 can be changed by the turning of a screw on a carbed motor. <P>My friend that just moved to cobb county from bartow has a 431RWhp built 351 in his 80 F150 4x4. he/Ed put an EGR plate under the carb and a 3" cat he passed emissions about 3 weeks ago. he has since removed these parts and the truck is back to being a PSYCHO beast. (Reck Neck John - he works at the shop)||||reg||1
